" r="2.5"/><circle cx="132" cy="114" r="2.5"/></g><circle cx="186" cy="58" r="18" fill="#f9a03f"/><circle cx="186" cy="58" r="12" fill="#ffc46b"/><path d="M178 20 l-10 70" stroke="#f07a5a" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><div><b>Fanta orange</b><p>Somehow even better ice-cold on a Mauritian beach.</p></div></div></div></div>
+<div class="fd-block"><p class="section-label">OUR SHORTLIST</p><h2>Where to eat</h2><div class="mo-grid"><div class="wh-col"><p class="mo-h">STREET FOOD</p><div class="wh-i"><a class="wh-n" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Dewa+and+Sons+Rose+Hill" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="wh-pin" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5A7 7 0 0 1 19 9.5C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg><b>Dewa &amp; Sons, Rose Hill</b></a><p>A famous dholl puri stop. Takeaway, cheap and always busy.</p></div><div class="wh-i"><a class="wh-n" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Port+Louis+Central+Market" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="wh-pin" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5A7 7 0 0 1 19 9.5C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg><b>Port Louis Central Market</b></a><p>Dholl puri, alouda and boulettes in one place. Go in the morning.</p></div><div class="wh-i"><a class="wh-n" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Shabaan+Kebab+Quatre+Bornes" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="wh-pin" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5A7 7 0 0 1 19 9.5C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg><b>Shabaan, Quatre Bornes</b></a><p>Often called the best pain kebab on the island. Expect a lunchtime queue; it’s worth it.</p></div></div><div class="wh-col"><p class="mo-h">SIT-DOWN LUNCHES</p><div class="wh-i"><a class="wh-n" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=First+Restaurant+China+Town+Port+Louis" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="wh-pin" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5A7 7 0 0 1 19 9.5C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg><b>First Restaurant, China Town</b></a><p>Busy Cantonese spot with lots of dim sum. Book on Sundays.</p></div><div class="wh-i"><a class="wh-n" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Escale+Creole+Moka" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="wh-pin" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5A7 7 0 0 1 19 9.5C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg><b>Escale Créole, Moka</b></a><p>Home-style Creole cooking in a garden, with homemade infused rums.</p></div><div class="wh-i"><a class="wh-n" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Maison+Eureka+Moka" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="wh-pin" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5A7 7 0 0 1 19 9.5C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg><b>Maison Eureka, Moka</b></a><p>Lunch on the veranda of a 180-year-old plantation house.</p></div><div class="wh-i"><a class="wh-n" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Dragon+Vert+Quatre+Bornes" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="wh-pin" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5A7 7 0 0 1 19 9.5C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg><b>Dragon Vert, Quatre Bornes</b></a><p>A family favourite for Chinese-Mauritian food. Try the Magic Bowl or the riz dragon.</p></div></div><div class="wh-col"><p class="mo-h">WITH A VIEW</p><div class="wh-i"><a class="wh-n" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=La+Table+du+Chateau+Labourdonnais" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="wh-pin" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5A7 7 0 0 1 19 9.5C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg><b>La Table du Château</b></a><p>At Château de Labourdonnais. Try the vanilla crème brûlée.</p></div><div class="wh-i"><a class="wh-n" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=L+Alchimiste+Rhumerie+de+Chamarel" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="wh-pin" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5A7 7 0 0 1 19 9.5C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg><b>L’Alchimiste, Chamarel</b></a><p>At the Rhumerie de Chamarel, with rum-laced desserts.</p></div><div class="wh-i"><a class="wh-n" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Le+Chamarel+Restaurant" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="wh-pin" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5A7 7 0 0 1 19 9.5C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg><b>Le Chamarel Restaurant</b></a><p>Lunch looking out to Le Morne and the sea.</p></div><div class="wh-i"><a class="wh-n" href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Domaine+Anna+Flic+en+Flac" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg class="wh-pin" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5A7 7 0 0 1 19 9.5C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg><b>Domaine Anna, Flic en Flac</b></a><p>Reimagined Chinese dishes and seafood, served in gazebos over the lakes. Also where our Mehendi is!</p></div></div></div></div>
