-			<section class="faq" id="faq" data-view="faq"><p class="section-label">FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS</p><h2>FAQ</h2><div class="toran diyas" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="faq-tabs" role="tablist"><button type="button" class="faq-tab" role="tab" data-p="faq-0" aria-selected="true">GETTING THERE</button><button type="button" class="faq-tab" role="tab" data-p="faq-1" aria-selected="false">WEATHER &amp; PACKING</button><button type="button" class="faq-tab" role="tab" data-p="faq-2" aria-selected="false">ATTIRE</button><button type="button" class="faq-tab" role="tab" data-p="faq-3" aria-selected="false">CELEBRATIONS</button></div><div class="faq-panel" role="tabpanel" id="faq-0"><details><summary>How do I get from the airport?</summary><p>The airport (MRU) is about an hour’s drive from Flic en Flac. Taxis and pre-booked transfers are easy to arrange. Group transfer details are coming soon.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need a visa or any forms?</summary><p>It depends on your passport. Many nationalities can enter visa-free for tourism, but please check the official Mauritius Passport and Immigration Office website for yours. Every traveller must also complete the free All-in-One Travel Digital Form on the <a href="https://safemauritius.govmu.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">official SafeMauritius site</a> before flying (currently at least 72 hours before arrival) and save the QR code to show on arrival.</p></details><details><summary>What about money and tipping?</summary><p>The local currency is the Mauritian rupee (MUR). Cards are widely accepted at hotels and restaurants, but carry some cash for markets and taxis. Tipping is appreciated but not expected.</p></details><details><summary>Can I drive?</summary><p>Cars drive on the left in Mauritius. Many visitors hire a driver for a day of sightseeing.</p></details><details><summary>Can I make a holiday of it?</summary><p>Absolutely. Have a look at our <a href="explore.html">Explore the Island</a> page for our favourite day trips.</p></details></div><div class="faq-panel" role="tabpanel" id="faq-1" hidden><details><summary>What’s the weather like in June?</summary><p>June is winter in Mauritius: sunny days in the mid-20s °C, cooler evenings and the odd shower. The sea is still lovely for swimming.</p></details><details><summary>What should I pack?</summary><p>Light layers, something warmer for the evenings, swimwear, a sun hat, sunscreen, insect repellent and comfortable shoes for sightseeing.</p></details><details><summary>Plugs, power &amp; phones?</summary><p>Sockets are Type C and G (230V), so UK plugs work. Mauritius is on GMT+4. Check your roaming charges, or pick up a local SIM or eSIM.</p></details></div><div class="faq-panel" role="tabpanel" id="faq-2" hidden><details><summary>What should I wear?</summary><p>Each celebration has its own suggested dress code and colours on the <a href="#itinerary">Events</a> page. Indian and Western attire are both welcome.</p></details><details><summary>Where can I get Indian outfits?</summary><p>Borrow from friends and family, buy online before you travel, or look to the tailors and shops in Mauritius (Port Louis is a good place to start). Details coming soon.</p></details></div><div class="faq-panel" role="tabpanel" id="faq-3" hidden><details><summary>Can I bring a plus-one or my children?</summary><p>We’ve named everyone we’re delighted to be celebrating with on your invitation. With a destination wedding and a limited guest list, we’re sadly not able to accommodate additional guests or plus-ones who weren’t included. Thank you so much for understanding. We can’t wait to celebrate with you!</p></details><details><summary>When should I RSVP by?</summary><p>Please RSVP by 15 January 2027.</p></details><details><summary>Gifts, or who do I contact with questions?</summary><p>Please message Sonali or Piers directly.</p></details></div><a class="view-next" href="#rsvp"><small>Up next</small><b>RSVP</b><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section>
